>	(shell file that uses awk)

Having spent that time thinking, one should realize that, like echo,
printf should be faster than starting up awk.  To do otherwise is
wasting someone's time.

Look, ``the UNIX philosophy'' does NOT mean bending existing utilities
to do poorly what a simple C program can do well.  It is perfectly
fine to prototype the function one wants using the suite of tools that
UNIX comes packaged with.  However, once you've done that prototype,
if you're going to make extensive use of it, translating a shell-file
into C is a perfectly acceptable optimization.


